Package: open-alert-base
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: open-ALERT <cdomotor-g@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: nodejs (>= 18.17), rtl-sdr, ca-certificates, adduser
Recommends: nftables
Suggests: socat
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/cdomotor-g/open-ALERT
Description: open-ALERT base station (flood-warning radio telemetry to Flood-Net)
 The RPi ALERT agent, unchanged from its signed release @TAG@, for any Debian
 or Ubuntu computer (x86-64 or 64-bit ARM). It decodes ALERT and ALERT2
 flood-warning radio telemetry from RTL-SDR USB sticks and serial receivers and
 posts the readings to Flood-Net over outbound HTTPS.
 .
 This package adds what a managed network asks for: a locked-down service with
 no root helper, two settings profiles (standard and enterprise), web-proxy
 support, the device rules for the sticks, and "open-alert-base audit", which
 prints the security posture for a reviewer.
 .
 Not yet tested with a real radio stick on hardware other than a Raspberry Pi.
